---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Contact | PH-Tools" activePage="contact">
  <div class="content-page">
    <h1>Contact &amp; help</h1>

    <h2>PH-Tools</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/">PH-Tools</a> is the umbrella for the open-source software we build for Passive House
      energy modeling. Honeybee-PH is our Grasshopper plugin, built on top of Honeybee and Ladybug Tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Get help</h2>
    <p>Having trouble? Check the links below first, and read <a href="#how-to-ask-for-help">How to ask for help</a> before posting.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Check <a href="/honeybee-ph/resources/">Resources</a> for walkthroughs and tutorials.</li>
      <li>Running into setup errors? See the <a href="/honeybee-ph/install/">Install</a> page.</li>
      <li>Rhino or Grasshopper questions: <a href="https://discourse.mcneel.com/" target="_blank">Rhino Forum</a>.</li>
      <li>
        Ladybug Tools, Honeybee, or Honeybee-PH questions:
        <a href="https://discourse.ladybug.tools/" target="_blank">Ladybug Tools Forum</a>.
        Posting publicly helps the next person who hits the same issue.
      </li>
      <li>Found a bug? Open a <a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_grasshopper_ph/issues" target="_blank">GitHub issue</a>.</li>
      <li>Still stuck? Email us at <a href="mailto:phtools@bldgtyp.com">phtools@bldgtyp.com</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-to-ask-for-help">How to ask for help</h2>
    <p>
      We're glad to help, but we need enough context to reproduce what you're seeing.
      Include these details in any forum post or email:
    </p>

    <h3>Current behavior</h3>
    <p>What is happening? Be specific about the step or component where things break.</p>

    <h3>Expected behavior</h3>
    <p>What did you expect to happen instead?</p>

    <h3>What you've tried</h3>
    <p>What steps have you already taken to troubleshoot it?</p>

    <h3>Environment details</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Operating system and version (Windows or macOS)</li>
      <li>Rhino version</li>
      <li>Ladybug Tools version</li>
      <li>PHPP version and language, if exporting to PHPP</li>
      <li>WUFI-Passive version, if exporting to WUFI-Passive</li>
      <li>Versions of any other relevant plugins</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Screenshots</h3>
    <p>We can't see your screen. Attach screenshots of the error message and the Grasshopper canvas around the problem.</p>

    <h3>Example files</h3>
    <p>Before sharing a Grasshopper file:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Internalize any linked data or files into the GH file, since we don't have access to your computer or network.</li>
      <li>Use the Ladybug Tools weather download component rather than hard-coded local paths.</li>
      <li>Internalize Rhino geometry. Geometry pipelines will break on another machine.</li>
      <li>Strip out third-party plugins. Keep only standard Grasshopper, Honeybee, and Honeybee-PH components.</li>
      <li>Trim the definition down to the smallest example that reproduces the bug. Half the time, doing this reveals the fix on its own.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contributing</h2>
    <p>
      Honeybee-PH is free and open-source. To contribute code, bug reports, or docs,
      start with the <a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/contributing" target="_blank">PH-Tools contributing guide</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:phtools@bldgtyp.com">phtools@bldgtyp.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Relevant links</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_grasshopper_ph" target="_blank">honeybee-grasshopper-ph</a>: Grasshopper components</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_ph" target="_blank">honeybee-ph</a>: Python data model</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/PHX" target="_blank">PHX</a>: WUFI-Passive and PHPP conversion engine</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
